            "review_text": "misskroft\nMoscow, Russia759 contributions\n0\nGood purity level for Da Nang, but the shrimp dish was disappointing.\nJul 2026 • Couples\nCompared to most of Da Nang's local establishments, this restaurant is really clean. In the hall, at tables and on the floor cleaned up, although, of course, this place still falls short of the usual standards of cleanliness in Russian restaurants. Very properly and hygienically organized toilet-sink is taken out, you can wash your hands comfortably.\nA nice plus in the service is that guests are given disposable aprons to avoid getting their clothes dirty when eating. Drinking water is also served here free of charge.\nRegarding the kitchen: ordered shrimp in garlic sauce, counting on the classics (roasted in butter with garlic). But they were brought in thick with cheese, apparently powdered. The dish didn't like it at all, it didn't meet expectations. But the roasted sea spinach is nicely cooked, nicely crisp. The drinks were fine, too.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten July 28, 2026",
